cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "aptahmm: a hidden Markov model based DNA aptamer sequence generator"
abstract: >-
  aptahmm fits a first-order discrete hidden Markov model to a curated set of
  experimentally validated single-stranded DNA aptamers and samples
  fixed-length candidate sequences from the fitted model. Candidates are
  ranked by a position-specific scoring matrix derived from the same seed set
  and filtered on GC content and homopolymer run length. The package also
  detects and removes the constant SELEX primer-binding regions that are
  commonly retained in published aptamer sequences, and reports the
  information criteria and per-sequence hidden-state occupancies needed to
  judge whether a given seed set supports the fitted model. The model encodes
  general sequence characteristics of SELEX-derived ssDNA aptamers and makes
  no claim of affinity for any particular molecular target.
